exceed/beyond and super-/ultra-/hyper-, and Korean 초. The second word of
'more than' responds much more than other upward comparisons. Longer words
containing an intensifying prefix usually get a weaker response than the
prefix by itself. A few weaker cues concern reaching a threshold or an
extreme. This is a lexical approximation: it does not recognize every phrase
with these meanings, and leaves unrelated activation near zero.
