"""layers.0.mlp.down_proj:603, read as a particle detector.

What it does: this component writes into the residual stream mostly when the current
token is a Japanese or Korean grammatical particle that marks a topic, a contrast, or a
condition. Its strongest response is the Japanese topic marker は and its compounds
(では, には, とは, 場合は, ...), then the "also" particle も (にも, でも), the Korean
topic particles 은/는 (and 도), and conditional endings such as れば, なら, たら, ても.
Plain case particles (の を に で と や) give a weak response, other hiragana a little,
the English past copula " was"/" were" a small one, and the demonstratives この/その/이
a negative one. Every other token predicts 0.

The program looks only at the current token, so it needs no carry between positions.
"""

